{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791051540,"nonce":"NNDa22jxQ4FmiaFspoQkdyCEnTk=","title":"Embed: a program imports a host's typed modules","message":"ZynML could not reach a host class (a Haxe or Wren class an embedder owns): it has no foreign import and no dynamic object type. Python could, through the typed host schemas in zyntax_python (HostModule, HostClass, HostMethod, HostField, HostType) and the foreign-object protocol. Caribou's gate needs a ZynML handler whose op calls Prompt.question(q) on a Haxe class.\n\nScope: the schema types move to zyntax_embed::host (zyntax_python re-exports them); TieredRuntime::add_host_modules takes a resolver from module path to HostModule; an import naming a host module (whole path, longest first) is replaced by typed declarations built as a TypedProgram in the embed layer, never as source: each class an extern type whose value is the foreign box, each member a generated function calling $Foreign$invoke/construct/get/set with arguments boxed and results unboxed at the declared types. A failed host call returns its type's zero and leaves the error for foreign::take_error.","files":null}]}